  "result": "Fixed: completion now keeps `#` as part of the argument instead of treating it as a comment. The tests in `tests/test_parser.py` and `tests/test_shell_completion.py` pass.\n\nThe cause was `split_arg_string` in `src/click/shell_completion.py`. It uses `shlex`, which by default treats `#` as the start of a comment and drops everything after it. I set `lex.commenters = \"\"` to turn that off.\n\nI added two cases to `test_split_arg_string` in `tests/test_parser.py`: `a#b` and a leading `#a`.\n\nI only ran those two test files, not the full suite.",
